  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming Teacher Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Zambia):  Over the years, works aimed at enhancing the quality of education in Zambia have predominantly focused on facilitating access and delivering school-based interventions with limited focus on the other core elements which are necessary for an effective and self-sustaining system. USAID will partner with the Government of the Republic of Zambia&apos;s (GRZ) Ministry of General Education (MOGE) to improve the capacity of universities and colleges of education to complement, strengthen, and sustain existing investments in early-grade reading. .The Transforming Teacher Education activity will make targeted, foundational investments to institutionalize early-grade reading expertise among faculties at the pre-service level, and devise a practical program of study to prepare teachers for teaching reading at the pre-primary and primary school levels. Using FY 2021 funds and in partnership with US based education institutions, it will directly target principals and lecturers to participate in an intensive course of study in language, literacy, early-grade reading, and differentiated instruction. The activity will also establish two Centers of Excellence housed at the University of Zambia and one of the colleges of education to sustain effective instructional practices, coaching, and mentoring in primary literacy instruction.The activity will complement USAID/Zambia&apos;s existing investments, primarily the Let&apos;s Read and Teaching at the Right Level (Catch Up) activities which focus on improving the instructional skills of in-service teachers already deployed to schools. This will support achievement of USAID/Zambia CDCS Development Objective 4: Quality of Primary Education Strengthened to Improve Learning Outcomes.It also contributes directly to the Administration policy priority of promoting healthy, educated, and productive populations in partner countries to drive inclusive and sustainable development and support U.S. prosperity and security objectives..</narrative>
  </description>
